{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>One who sacrifices to elohim.</b> According to the plain sense, it does not speak of Israel, for they were already warned in the Decalogue: 'You shall have no other.' Rather, it speaks only of the convert mentioned after it; and for his sake too it is stated, 'whoever lies with a beast,' for such is the custom of Arameans." "<b>Except to HaShem alone.</b> This teaches that if one slaughtered to HaKadosh Barukh Hu and to other elohim as well — like the Cutheans, about whom it is written, 'they feared HaShem and served their elohim' — since he worships in partnership, he is condemned to ḥerem; therefore it says לבדו, 'alone.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:59:51.047916676Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}